From d5bdccc195a7f53624257daa2d2600057227c80c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:44:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 115/117] i2c: mediatek: support MT6797 iDVFS transfer format

The MT6797 iDVFS I2C instance packs WRRD lengths as an eight-bit transmit
field and a five-bit receive field. Its vendor path also uses the
eight-byte controller FIFO for short transfers instead of starting the
I2C6 APDMA channel.

Add dedicated nonzero and length quirks, encode the packed lengths, and
select FIFO only when each transfer leg fits. Use the vendor's 32-bit
DATA_PORT accesses and require an exact receive count before copying FIFO
data.

Reject arbitration loss and every non-exact completion status on this
special controller. Keep the ordinary MT6797-to-MT8173 match and its DMA
path unchanged.

---
